It implements interval methods published by others; see the citations printed in
every report and in README.md (Morris & Lobsenz 2000; Donner & Zou 2012;
Newcombe 2016; Wilson 1927; Koopman 1984; Miettinen & Nurminen 1985; Katz et al. 1978).

The worked examples in examples/ use public data: a Michigan single-lender HMDA
filing (CFPB/FFIEC public HMDA data) and the ProPublica COMPAS Broward County data
(https://github.com/propublica/compas-analysis). Those datasets remain subject to
their publishers' terms. Only aggregate counts are included here.
